  "question": {
    "text": "Three forces $\\vec{P}, \\vec{Q}$ and $\\vec{R}$ acting along IA, IB and IC, where I is the incentre of a $\\triangle A B C$, are in equilibrium. Then $\\vec{P}: \\vec{Q}: \\vec{R}$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "BsYB2",
      "text": "\n$\\cos \\frac{A}{2}: \\cos \\frac{B}{2}: \\cos \\frac{C}{2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "uHXxN",
      "text": "\n$\\sin \\frac{A}{2}: \\sin \\frac{B}{2}: \\sin \\frac{C}{2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "S8TZn",
      "text": "\n$\\sec \\frac{A}{2}: \\sec \\frac{B}{2}: \\sec \\frac{C}{2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "4HAqS",
      "text": "\n$\\operatorname{cosec} \\frac{A}{2}: \\operatorname{cosec} \\frac{B}{2}: \\operatorname{cosec} \\frac{C}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "By Lami's theorem\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\vec{P}: \\vec{Q}: \\vec{R}=\\sin \\left(90^{\\circ}+\\frac{A}{2}\\right): \\sin \\left(90^{\\circ}+\\frac{B}{2}\\right): \\sin \\left(90^{\\circ}+\\frac{C}{2}\\right) \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\cos \\frac{A}{2}: \\cos \\frac{B}{2}: \\cos \\frac{C}{2} .\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/EJGWEbzIzvbKED_KCAj_rG8c6xAHxABi4MG2luhcbUo.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
